From: Water500ton <Water500ton@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] net: ipa: add SM8750 (IPA v5.5) endpoint, SRAM, and QMI SMEM TLV support

Add Qualcomm SM8750 (Pakala) IPA v5.5 support (`qcom,sm8750-ipa`) verified
on Realme GT7 Pro (`pista`, RMX5010) with live 5G NR SA (`n78` 100 MHz)
and 4G LTE cellular data via `rmnet_ipa0` + `rmnet.ko` (QMAPv5):

- Add `ipa_data_v5_5_sm8750` endpoint and IPA SRAM partition tables
  (`AP_LAN_RX` ch14/ep17, `AP_MODEM_RX` ch1/ep24, `MODEM_AP_RX` ch7/ep22;
  non-overlapping SM8750 filter/stats/modem/NAT/PDN SRAM layout).
- Retain the SMEM physical address and allocated size from `ipa_smem_init()`.
- Extend `QMI_IPA_INIT_MODEM_DRIVER_REQ` (`IPA_QMI_INIT_DRIVER_REQ_SZ` = 197)
  with the three IPA v5.5 SM8750 TLVs (`0x23` `hw_filter_stats`, `0x24`
  `ipa_smem_info`, and `0x25` `smem_info`) required by SM8750 MPSS firmware
  to avoid `IPA_SMEM_ALLOC_EX` assertion during modem IPA QMI handshake.

---
